n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-x(vx)+(vx)^{2}}{(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(1-v+{v}^{2})}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activi