) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3{v}^{3}{x}^{3}}{v{x}^{3}(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{3{v}^{3}\\cancel{{x}^{3}}}{v\\cancel{{x}^{3}}(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}}{v+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}}{v+1}-\\frac{v(v+1)}{v+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{v}^{2}-{v}^{2}-v}{v+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2{v}^{2}-v}{v+1} \\\\ (\\frac{v+1}{2{v}^{2}-v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9eeb606c069aa5226f07b04ddcdb323200004270309fc007d683aeb98aecf5"} {"question" "q-14315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{2{v}^{2}-v}{v+1})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x"] ["math" "(\\frac{v+1}{2{v}^{2}-v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "(\\frac{v+1}{2{v}^{3}-{v}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x"] ["math" "(\\frac{v+1}{{v}^{2}+1})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "(\\frac{{v}^{2}+v}{3{v}^{2}-v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{v+1}{2{v}^{2}-v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})+\\frac{3y}{x}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})+\\frac{3y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{v}^{2}{x}^{2}})+\\frac{3vx}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+3v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v \\\\ (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14314" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9eeb606c069aa5226f07b04ddcdb323200004270309fc007d683aeb98aecf5"} {"question" "q-14314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})+v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{v})+2{v}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}))\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x"] ["math" "(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14314" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}})+2v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+2y}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+2y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{x+2(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{x(1+2v)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =1+2v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =1+v \\\\ \\frac{1}{1+v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{1+v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v+1| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v+1| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{{C}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v+1| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{{C}_{1}}|x|) \\\\ |v+1| & ={e}^{{C}_{1}}|x| \\\\ v+1 & =\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}}x \\\\ v+1 & =Cx \\\\ v & =Cx-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have let $C=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x} & =Cx-1 \\\\ y & =C{x}^{2}-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9eeb606c069aa5226f07b04ddcdb323200004270309fc007d683aeb98aecf5"} {"question" "q-90692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=C{x}^{2}+2x"] ["math" "y=C{x}^{2}-x"] ["math" "y=C{x}^{3}+x"] ["math" "y=C{x}^{3}-2x"] ["math" "y=C{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=C{x}^{2}-x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{3})}{{v}^{2}{x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}}+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ {v}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {v}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+3{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have let $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{3} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{{x}^{3}} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C) \\\\ y & =x\\sqrt[3]{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9eeb606c069aa5226f07b04ddcdb323200004270309fc007d683aeb98aecf5"} {"question" "q-90691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=x(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)"] ["math" "y=x\\sqrt[3]{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}"] ["math" "y=x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}"] ["math" "y=x{(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)}^{2}"] ["math" "y={x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=x\\sqrt[3]{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is a homogeneous equation because it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y),\n$$\n\nand we notice that all terms in the numerator and denominator of $f(x,y)$ are of order $3$ (i.e., they are cubic).\n\nUsing the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{3}+x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)+{x}^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}({v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1)}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1-{v}^{3}-{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v+1}{v(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{v} \\\\ v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int v\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9eeb606c069aa5226f07b04ddcdb323200004270309fc007d683aeb98aecf5"} {"question" "q-14321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=x(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)"] ["math" "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)"] ["math" "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)"] ["math" "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-14321" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-8844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{xy}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-8844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is a homogeneous equation because it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y),\n$$\n\nand we notice that all terms in the numerator and denominator of $f(x,y)$ are of order $2$ (i.e., they are quadratic).\n\nUsing the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{xy} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{2}-{x}^{2}}{x(vx)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}-1)}{v{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{2}-1}{v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{2}-1-{v}^{2}}{v} \\\\ v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int v\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+C{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-8844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9eeb606c069aa5226f07b04ddcdb323200004270309fc007d683aeb98aecf5"} {"question" "q-8844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-8844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+C{x}^{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-{x}^{3}+C{x}^{2}"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C{x}^{3}+x)"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C{x}^{3}"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+Cx)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-8844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+C{x}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}{x}^{3}}{({v}^{2}+1){x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (v+\\frac{1}{v})\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v| & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v| & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({v}^{2}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}) & =C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})} & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa9eeb606c069aa5226f07b04ddcdb323200004270309fc007d683aeb98aecf5"} {"question" "q-90688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{C+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}={x}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}=4x"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{C+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}=2{x}^{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}={x}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{y}^{4}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}=2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "q-90688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})}={x}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d14fe70966ea9768012cec677886136e9f2551f40183c63dcddea8b520b2772"} {"question" "e-2393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{x}$\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{x^2}$\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{y}{2x}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^2}\\right)}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/example-2393.json" "file_sha256" "cd83638721bea398d3863d0fd5e88389107c3149a8441b073ab28d4a1ac8d935"} {"question" "e-2393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    f(x, y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero, meaning that it satisfies\n\n$$\nf(tx, ty) = f(x, y).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at the right-hand side function in each differential equation.\n\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{x}$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(ty)}{(tx)} \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{t\\cdot y}{t\\cdot x} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, equation I is a homogenous differential equation.\n\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{x^2}$ is *not* a homogeneous function of degree $0.$ Rather, it is a homogeneous function of degree $-1\\mathbin{:}$\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(ty)}{(tx)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{t\\cdot y}{{t}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & ={t}^{-1}f(x,y)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, equation II is *not* a homogenous differential equation.\n\n- The function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{y}{2x}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{x^2}{y^2}\\right)}$ is a homogeneous function of degree zero:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{ty}{2(tx)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{(tx)^{2}}{(ty)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\text{ }\\frac{t\\cdot y}{t\\cdot 2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{t}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{t}^{2}{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, equation III is a homogenous differential equation.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/example-2393.json" "file_sha256" "cd83638721bea398d3863d0fd5e88389107c3149a8441b073ab28d4a1ac8d935"} {"question" "e-2301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use the transformation $y = vx$  (where $v=v(x)$) to rewrite the given first-order homogeneous ODE \n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}    =   \\cos \\left( \\frac {y} {x} \\right)\n$$\n\nas a separable ODE in $v$ and $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/example-2301.json" "file_sha256" "abaa709284cebc9ac03a2769297fb1ceaf075e2fe714e20599a7b6507e04b16e"} {"question" "e-2301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "With $y = vx$ (where $v = v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging that into the differential equation and separating variables, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(v) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(v)-v \\\\ (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(v)-v})\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044192/example-2301.json" "file_sha256" "abaa709284cebc9ac03a2769297fb1ceaf075e2fe714e20599a7b6507e04b16e"} {"question" "e-2302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gen